    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen `'autocomplete'` is enabled, there is no way to have the first completion candidate selected/highlighted without also inserting its text into the buffer.\n\nFor example:\n\n```lua\nvim.o.autocomplete = true\nvim.o.complete = \".\"\nvim.opt.completeopt = { \"menuone\", \"noinsert\" }\n```\n\nGiven a buffer containing `print`, when I type `pri` elsewhere I would like the completion menu to highlight `print` while leaving the buffer text as `pri`.\n\nInstead, `\"noinsert\"` has no effect under `'autocomplete'`. The available behaviors are effectively:\n\n- `\"noselect\"`: the buffer is unchanged, but no item is selected.\n- `\"preselect\"` or implicit selection: an item is selected, but its completion text is also inserted/previewed.\n\nThis leaves no native equivalent of the common completion behavior:\n\n```text\nfirst item highlighted\nbuffer text unchanged\nCTRL-Y accepts the highlighted item\n```\n\nCompletion plugins expose selection and insertion independently. For example, blink.cmp supports:\n\n```lua\nselection = {\n  preselect = true,\n  auto_insert = false,\n}\n```\n\nThe existing `\"noinsert\"` flag already describes the desired behavior for regular Insert-mode completion, but the documentation states that it has no effect when `'autocomplete'` is enabled.\n\nSearch terms used when checking existing issues:\n\n- autocomplete noinsert\n- autocomplete preselect noinsert\n- completion select without insert\n- native completion auto insert\n- completeopt noinsert\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nWhen `'completeopt'` contains `\"noinsert\"` and `'autocomplete'` opens the completion menu:\n\n1. The first candidate is selected/highlighted.\n2. Text after the typed prefix is not inserted or previewed in the buffer.\n3. `CTRL-Y` accepts and inserts the selected candidate.\n4. Continuing to type keeps filtering the completion list normally.\n5. `CTRL-E` dismisses completion while preserving the text typed by the user.\n\nFor example, with `print` available as a candidate:\n\n```text\nTyped buffer:    pri\nSelected item:   print\nVisible buffer:  pri\n```\n\nAfter pressing `CTRL-Y`:\n\n```text\nVisible buffer:  print\n```\n\nIf both `\"noselect\"` and `\"noinsert\"` are present, `\"noselect\"` can continue to take precedence, matching the existing documented behavior.\n\nThis would not change the default behavior. It would only make the existing `\"noinsert\"` flag effective when explicitly configured with `'autocomplete'`.\n",
